{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3298","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3298","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3298\",\"parent_revision\":\"3105a032324f03f0aaf731af1810db489c72997b995c844f81d4a1e31fdc4381\",\"root_revision\":\"3105a032324f03f0aaf731af1810db489c72997b995c844f81d4a1e31fdc4381\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-29\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nFollow-up from #3277's documentation-drift audit, capturing two out-of-scope audit recommendations so they are not lost.\\n\\n1. `complete-implementation/SKILL.md`'s Pre-Phase 1 TN Verification Check treats an absent `TN-verification` artifact the same as \\\"no structured criteria to verify\\\" \u2014 it does not distinguish that case from \\\"structured criteria existed but were never verified,\\\" so a plan with real acceptance criteria whose TN task never ran can silently pass through. #3277 wires `BookendValidator` into `create_plan`/`finalize_plan` so this can no longer happen for plans created after that fix, except plans that were already in `state=ready` before the fix shipped, which are exempted from the new gate and could still hit this ambiguity.\\n\\n2. Confirm that `swarm-task-planner`'s bookend-generation step is not itself ever the source of a plan reaching a non-compliant `ready` state, now that #3277's schema-level enforcement rejects any such plan at write time regardless of what the planning agent does. #3277's own grooming already ran a 5-Whys root-cause analysis and found the original defect was a code/schema wiring gap (BookendValidator never wired into any write path), not an agent-instruction gap \u2014 swarm-task-planner's documented bookend-generation instructions were independently fact-checked and found correct. This item exists only to confirm that conclusion still holds and close the audit's open recommendation; it is not a re-investigation.\\n\\n**Hypothesis**: Item 2 is likely no-op / closable without further action, since #3277's enforcement makes the planner's own behavior unable to produce a non-compliant ready plan either way.\\n\\n**User-provided context**: Suggested fix for item 1 (from the doc-drift audit) \u2014 when the TN-verification artifact is absent, read the plan's `acceptance_criteria_structured` field directly rather than assuming its absence means no criteria exist: if populated, stop and report that verification was never captured, rather than silently proceeding.\\n\\nSource: doc-drift-auditor audit report registered against #3277 (Priority 1 and Priority 3 recommendations, deliberately deferred out of #3277's scope per that item's architect spec \u00a74/\u00a78 and Root-Cause Analysis section).\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Agent task - QG T5 doc-drift audit follow-up on #3277 (bookend-validator-wiring)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-29\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"e1d435d19bdf6ad19d7dbf8cea3e0852c75ff395603d7ceec86f669114d65e6e\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRZ5l6g\"}"}